                  "type": {
                    "definition": "user-data-type",
                    "value": "RGB"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "documentation": "Cell chemistry classification from OCV and internal resistance (IR).\n\n   Each chemistry has a typical OCV and IR with a 1-sigma spread. A reading\n   is scored by its squared normalised distance from each profile:\n     score = ((OCV - typ) / sigma)^2 + IR_WEIGHT * (ln(IR / typ) / ln(k))^2\n   IR is compared on a log scale because it varies by multiples, not\n   offsets. The lowest score wins; above MAX_MATCH_SCORE the cell is\n   unknown. With IR_VALID false the cell is classified on OCV alone.",
              "extensible": false
            },
            "variable": {
              "name": "classifier",
              "class": "local",
              "type": {
                "definition": "user-data-type",
                "value": "CELL_CLASSIFIER"
