                {
                  "name": "LED_B",
                  "class": "input",
                  "type": {
                    "definition": "base-type",
                    "value": "USINT"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "documentation": "ESP32-C3 output image: the electronic load setpoint and the on-board\n   WS2812 LED. Call last in the scan.\n\n   The load setpoint is a 20 kHz, 10-bit PWM on GPIO_1, RC-filtered to a DC\n   voltage on the op-amp (+) input. The op-amp drives the MOSFET so the same\n   voltage appears across RL. OpenPLC's generic analogue outputs run their\n   PWM at 4 kHz, which would leave ~5x the ripple on that voltage.\n     GPIO_1  PWM -> 47k series, 100nF to GND -> op-amp (+) input.\n             tau 4.7 ms, fc 33.9 Hz. At 20 kHz the ripple is ~4.5 mV p-p\n             at 0.5 V out; a step settles to 0.1% in ~33 ms (7 tau).\n   The LED on GPIO_8 is addressable, which plain digital outputs can't\n   drive. Keep GPIO 1 and 8 out of the board's pin mapping.\n\n   Needs the arduino-esp32 3.x core, which OpenPLC's ESP32 HAL also\n   requires. Does nothing on other targets.",
              "extensible": false
            },
            "variable": {
              "name": "outputs",
              "class": "local",
              "type": {
                "definition": "user-data-type",
                "value": "ESP32C3_OUTPUTS"
              },
              "location": "",
              "initialValue": null,
              "documentation": "",
              "debug": false
            },
